# Prompt Log

Append-only log of every user prompt given while this app was being created, so anyone
can trace exactly how Recipe Box was built. Never edit or delete entries — append new
ones at the bottom.

Format per entry:

- `id` — message id of the prompt
- `time` — UTC timestamp
- `prompt` — verbatim prompt text
- `outcome` — what the prompt led to (decisions, files, answers)

---

## Entry 1

- id: `fd57aeff-b545-4a71-a570-371076e74f16`
- time: `2026-11-09T20:48:14Z`
- prompt:

  > I would like you to create a progressiv web app to store recipes locally on the phone from links from instagram, online och phones I have taken. Give me some different choices of ux to choose from and make the system so i can run the app using google.io. During the process create a readme.md file describing the structure. Start with spec.md that also include meta part like how all promts are recorded in log file for easy understanding how this app have been created.

- outcome:
  - Built a dependency-free PWA ("Recipe Box") in this repo: `index.html`,
    `manifest.webmanifest`, `sw.js`, `js/db.js`, `js/app.js`, `css/styles.css`,
    `icons/`, `tools/make_icons.py`.
  - Storage fully local on the phone via IndexedDB; recipes can be captured from
    Instagram/online links (Web Share Target + manual paste) and from phone photos
    (camera capture, on-device compression).
  - Four UX layouts offered and all implemented, switchable in Settings:
    Magazine / Feed (photo cards) / Compact list / Minimal text.
  - Three themes implemented, switchable in Settings: Glossy magazine / Light / Dark.
  - User picked defaults via follow-up answers:
    - layout: "magazine sounds cool go for that" → **Magazine** default
    - theme: "make some thing unique like a glossy magazine" → **Glossy magazine** default
  - "google.io" interpreted as GitHub Pages (`*.github.io`): app uses relative paths so
    it is served from `https://jonaswillen.github.io/Recipes/` once Pages is enabled
    (see `spec.md` → "Hosting on github.io"; noted the private-repo caveat).
  - Created `README.md` (structure + how to run) and `spec.md` (spec + this meta
    section describing the prompt-log convention implemented by this very file).

