## Entry 2

- id: `b2e43615-ff93-4a31-ad3c-784a64dbdb02`
- time: `2026-11-09T21:14:25Z`
- prompt:

  > I thing a change every thing at github to make the commit avialable using github.io can you check or do everything looks good?

- outcome:
  - Verified repo state via `gh`/API: `main` and `vibe/recipe-pwa-0b572b` both at
    `83135cc`; repo is now **public** (`visibility: PUBLIC`), so Pages works on GitHub
    Free (private repos need a paid plan and are unpublished on Free).
  - Verified Pages is **not enabled**: `GET /repos/JonasWillen/Recipes/pages` → 404 and
    `https://jonaswillen.github.io/Recipes/` → "Site not found" 404.
  - Enabling Pages is a repo-settings change; mutating GitHub API calls are blocked in
    this session (`gh api -X POST …/pages` → "Mutating GitHub API calls are not
    allowed"), so the one-click enable must be done in the web UI — exact steps written
    into `spec.md` and `README.md` (set default branch to `main`, then Settings → Pages →
    deploy branch `main` from root).
  - Confirmed the app itself is Pages-ready for the `/Recipes/` project path: `index.html`
    and `.nojekyll` at root, all asset links relative, manifest `scope: "./"`,
    share-target action `./share-target`, SW registered as `sw.js`; all 16 paths served
    HTTP 200 from a loopback server smoke test.
  - Updated `spec.md` / `README.md` hosting sections with the verified status and steps.
